pkg:Evidence_v1_10_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.10.0 (MINOR release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: user gave the go-ahead to run planning and asked precisely whether this package has real deployment packages. Answered by checking BRSF's own Package class fresh: 'a deployable business function, released as a unit' with hasPackageVersion -- exactly what this package's own git-tag-per-release history already is (9 real releases shipped this session alone). None exists yet for this Epic's own work specifically, since nothing has shipped -- correctly not fabricated. Ran the actual planning ceremony: CostEstimate (Basis_Judged, honest for a first-ever iteration with no historical velocity) on all 5 Stories; opened Iteration 1 (capacity 5, 2 real weeks, dated to today); given the dependency chain is linear, only STORY-1 is unblocked and its own estimate (5) exactly fills the declared capacity -- committed via a real PlanningEvent. Real SHACL violations surfaced and fixed as found, not pre-empted: the Iteration needed hasIdentifier and a real member; the PlanningEvent needed producesTask (a real ExecutionTask, Task_Implementation per ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207); the new Task then needed its own identifier, state, and DoD. Learned by testing rather than assumed: ExecutionTask is a pipeline-tracked Backlog-stage type (unlike Iteration/PlanningEvent/CostEstimate), so adding one genuinely changed the Stage_Backlog digest -- recomputed and re-closed correctly. Re-verified after every fix: pipeline order (31 subjects, reproduces), full SHACL 0 violations."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "290cddce2bef4cae24f720c402109e63d63fcd215868c5bb322410b403bb3f81"^^xsd:string .
